Scorebug at mobile: team blocks 108 each + clock 74 + gaps 26 + padding 22 = 338; scale .85 => 287. Fine. But hud-right 38*2+gap=82, hud-left hidden. .hud-top justify-between with scorebug center and hud-right right; margin? Scorebug at x 48? If scorebug 287 and hud-right 82, total 369 plus padding 34 = 403 > 390. Overflows. Need reduce padding or reposition.

At max-width 680: `.hud-top{padding:12px?}` not set. Could set `.hud-top{padding:8px 8px}` and `.scorebug{transform:scale(.7)}`, team blocks 100, clock 62 maybe. Also `.hud-right` could be absolute top right. But game is small anyway.

Better mobile game design: allow scorebug centered, move HUD-right buttons to bottom-right or overlay top-right with smaller size. Since scorebug width 287 and hud-right 82, at 390 no room. We could hide `.hud-right` on mobile (pause accessible via Esc/P or pause button missing...). Not good. Could place hud-right at bottom-right with style-hud? Or reduce scorebug scale to .68: 338*.68=230, plus 82 + padding 16 = 328 fits 390. Use transform-origin top left, position? The scorebug is centered in flex; with hud-right it's pushed left. Let's set `.hud-top{gap:8px;padding:8px 10px}` `.scorebug{transform:scale(.68);transform-origin:top left}` `.hud-right{padding-top:0}` and `.team-block{min-width:100px}` maybe. That gives scorebug 230, hud-right 82, padding 20, gap 8 => 340. Fits.

But screenshot field is tiny due to aspect fit: world 1440x810 in 390x844 => scale .27, field width 349 and height 165, centered vertically at 312. Could make canvas fill width but field still 165 tall. On portrait, it's inevitable. Best played landscape message. Could add a rotate hint but not required.

At 390x844, the canvas aspect ratio letterboxes huge top/bottom black. Maybe instead we could show a dedicated mobile control overlay or encourage landscape. It's okay.

But scorebug clipping and hud-right offscreen should fix. Also the field y-center is 422 (screen), style-hud bottom 765, controls hidden. Fine.

Test landscape 844x390 to ensure game HUD works. We'll resize later.

Let's apply mobile HUD fixes:
```
@media (max-width:680px){
  .hud-top{padding:8px 10px;gap:8px}
  .scorebug{transform:scale(.68);transform-origin:top left}
  .hud-right{gap:4px;padding-top:0}
  .hud-icon{width:32px;height:32px;font-size:12px}
  .style-hud{min-width:150px}
}
```
But scorebug transform scale leaves layout width unchanged (transform doesn't affect layout), so flex layout still reserves 338 width and causes overflow! Indeed transform scale only visual, layout size remains. Need use `zoom` or set width? Transform origin doesn't change layout. That's why current scale .85 didn't prevent overflow. Use CSS `zoom`? Better actual smaller sizes: set `.team-block{min-width:0}` and hide team-names small or name? On mobile, show badge+score only, hide .team-names. Then scorebug width: 31+18+5 + clock 74 + 31+18 + gaps 26 + padding 22 = 225. Good. So at mobile:
```
.team-names{display:none}
.team-block{min-width:0}
.scorebug{transform:none;gap:8px;padding:6px 8px}
.match-clock{min-width:64px;padding:0 8px}
.hud-top{padding:8px 10px;gap:8px}
```
Hud-left hidden. Scorebug 31+18+8+64+8+31+18+16=194. With hud-right 82 + gap + padding, fits.

But hiding team names on mobile is acceptable for gameplay. Or keep only `b` names and hide small? Width would still ~59+44. Better hide names entirely for compact. The score bug with badges and scores is clear enough.

Also mobile field is tiny; but acceptable with message.

Apply.

